/*!
@defgroup fee
@ingroup mod_flash Asynchronous Flash EEPROM Emulation (FEE)
@brief Flash-backed logical block storage module for the YTMicro SDK.

@details
The Flash EEPROM Emulation (FEE) module stores application data as logical
blocks inside flash memory and presents an EEPROM-like programming model to the
upper software layers. The implementation uses cluster metadata, validation
flags, and background scan or swap jobs to maintain the newest valid copy of
each logical block while delegating physical flash access to the FLS backend.

@section fee_features Key Features
- Stores user data as configured logical blocks with per-block size, ownership,
  and immediate-data attributes.
- Uses cluster headers and block headers to track valid, invalid, inconsistent,
  and never-written block states.
- Supports asynchronous read, write, invalidate, and maintenance operations
  driven by Fee_MainFunction().
- Integrates the FLS backend through the module configuration so Fee_Init()
  initializes the required flash driver instance directly.
- Provides reserved-area handling for immediate blocks during cluster swap.
- Supports a reduced-overhead light mode and a full standard mode build.

@section fee_modes Supported Modes

| Mode | Enable Condition | Behavior |
|------|------------------|----------|
| Standard Mode | `FEE_LIGHT_MODE` undefined or `0` | Uses full block and cluster metadata, supports Fee_InvalidateBlock() and Fee_EraseImmediateBlock(), and keeps separate validation / invalidation flag areas. |
| Light Mode | `FEE_LIGHT_MODE == 1` | Uses reduced metadata overhead, serializes 24-bit flash addresses, and removes the invalidate / erase-immediate public services. |

@section fee_arch Module Architecture

@verbatim
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                  Application Code                   │
│       (calls Fee_Init / Fee_Read / Fee_Write)       │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│                 FEE Driver Layer                    │
│  ● Public API in fee.h / fee.c                      │
│  ● Logical block management, status reporting       │
│  ● Scan, swap, validation, and reserved-area flow   │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│              FEE Internal Job Pipeline              │
│  ● Header serialization / parsing helpers           │
│  ● Cluster scan state machine                       │
│  ● Cluster swap and block migration jobs            │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│              FLS Async Driver Layer                 │
│  ● Flash read / write / erase scheduling            │
│  ● Job completion callbacks back into FEE           │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│                Flash Memory Hardware                │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
@endverbatim

@subsection fee_arch_driver Driver Layer
Application code uses the public API declared in fee.h. Requests are accepted
as asynchronous jobs and complete only after Fee_MainFunction() advances the
internal state machine to MEMIF_IDLE.

@subsection fee_arch_jobs Internal Job Pipeline
The internal scheduler manages cluster discovery during initialization, parses
flash metadata, moves valid blocks during swap, and commits validation or
invalidation markers after each flash operation completes.

@subsection fee_arch_fls FLS Backend Contract
The `flashConfigPtr` field of Fee_ModuleUserConfig_t provides the FLS
configuration used by Fee_Init(). That FLS configuration must route its job-end
and job-error callbacks to Fee_JobEndNotification() and
Fee_JobErrorNotification().

@section fee_config Configuration Parameters

@subsection fee_config_module Fee_ModuleUserConfig_t Fields
| Field | Type | Description | Default / Source |
|-------|------|-------------|------------------|
| blockCnt | `uint16_t` | Number of logical blocks described by `blockConfigPtr`. | Board configuration |
| clusterCnt | `uint8_t` | Number of configured cluster groups. | Board configuration |
| clusterConfigPtr | `const Fee_ClusterGroupType *` | Pointer to the cluster-group table used by the FEE runtime. | Board configuration |
| blockConfigPtr | `const Fee_BlockConfigType *` | Pointer to the logical-block table used to resolve block IDs and sizes. | Board configuration |
| flashConfigPtr | `const Fls_ConfigType *` | Pointer to the FLS configuration that Fee_Init() forwards to Fls_Init(). | Board configuration |

@subsection fee_config_block Fee_BlockConfigType Fields
| Field | Type | Description |
|-------|------|-------------|
| BlockNumber | `uint16_t` | Public logical block identifier used by Fee_Read(), Fee_Write(), and maintenance APIs. |
| BlockSize | `uint16_t` | Payload size in bytes for the block. |
| ClrGrp | `uint8_t` | Cluster-group index that stores the block. |
| ImmediateData | `bool` | Marks the block as immediate data that uses reserved-area handling. |
| BlockAssignment | `Fee_BlockAssignmentType` | Declares whether the block belongs to shared, application, or bootloader storage. |

@subsection fee_config_cluster Fee_ClusterGroupType and Fee_ClusterType Fields
| Structure | Field | Type | Description |
|-----------|-------|------|-------------|
| Fee_ClusterGroupType | ClrPtr | `const Fee_ClusterType *const` | Pointer to the cluster list owned by the group. |
| Fee_ClusterGroupType | ClrCount | `uint32_t` | Number of clusters in the group. |
| Fee_ClusterGroupType | ReservedSize | `Fls_LengthType` | Bytes reserved for immediate-data updates while swap is active. |
| Fee_ClusterType | StartAddr | `Fls_AddressType` | Start address of the physical cluster in flash. |
| Fee_ClusterType | Length | `Fls_LengthType` | Cluster size in bytes. |

@subsection fee_config_macros Build-Time Feature Switches
| Macro | Description |
|-------|-------------|
| `FEE_LIGHT_MODE` | Selects reduced-overhead light mode when set to `1`. |
| `FEE_VERSION_INFO_API` | Enables Fee_GetVersionInfo() when set to `STD_ON`. |
| `FEE_NUMBER_OF_CLUSTER_GROUPS` | Number of cluster groups generated by the board configuration. |
| `FEE_CRT_CFG_NR_OF_BLOCKS` | Number of logical blocks generated by the board configuration. |
| `FEE_VIRTUAL_PAGE_SIZE` | Alignment unit used by the logical block layout. |
| `FEE_DATA_BUFFER_SIZE` | Size of the shared internal data buffer used by scan and swap jobs. |

@section fee_usage Usage Patterns

@subsection fee_usage_init Pattern 1: Initialize the Driver and Wait for the Initial Scan
Use this pattern during system startup. Fee_Init() schedules the initial scan
immediately, so the application must keep polling until the module becomes idle.

@code{.c}
#include "sdk_project_config.h"

static void Fee_WaitUntilIdle(void)
{
    while (Fee_GetStatus() != MEMIF_IDLE)
    {
        Fee_MainFunction();
    }
}

void App_InitStorage(void)
{
    Fee_Init(&Fee_ModuleConfig);
    Fee_WaitUntilIdle();
}
@endcode

@subsection fee_usage_rw Pattern 2: Write a Full Block and Read It Back
Accepted read and write requests are asynchronous. Poll Fee_MainFunction() after
each accepted request until the module returns to MEMIF_IDLE.

@code{.c}
#include "sdk_project_config.h"

uint8_t txBuffer[32] = {0x10U, 0x20U, 0x30U, 0x40U};
uint8_t rxBuffer[32] = {0U};

static void Fee_WaitUntilIdle(void)
{
    while (Fee_GetStatus() != MEMIF_IDLE)
    {
        Fee_MainFunction();
    }
}

void App_UpdateCounterBlock(void)
{
    if (Fee_Write(FeeConf_FeeBlockConfiguration_FeeBlockConfiguration_0,
                  txBuffer) == E_OK)
    {
        Fee_WaitUntilIdle();
    }

    if (Fee_Read(FeeConf_FeeBlockConfiguration_FeeBlockConfiguration_0,
                 0U,
                 rxBuffer,
                 sizeof(rxBuffer)) == E_OK)
    {
        Fee_WaitUntilIdle();
    }
}
@endcode

@subsection fee_usage_periodic Pattern 3: Periodic Background Processing in a Super Loop
When FEE is used by application tasks over time, poll the module regularly and
gate new requests on MEMIF_IDLE.

@code{.c}
void App_MainLoop(void)
{
    for (;;)
    {
        Fee_MainFunction();

        if (Fee_GetStatus() == MEMIF_IDLE)
        {
            /* Queue the next read or write request here. */
        }
    }
}
@endcode

@subsection fee_usage_maint Pattern 4: Standard-Mode Block Maintenance
Standard mode adds logical-block invalidation and immediate-block erase support.

@code{.c}
#if !defined(FEE_LIGHT_MODE) || (FEE_LIGHT_MODE == 0U)
static void Fee_WaitUntilIdle(void)
{
    while (Fee_GetStatus() != MEMIF_IDLE)
    {
        Fee_MainFunction();
    }
}

void App_RefreshImmediateBlock(void)
{
    if (Fee_EraseImmediateBlock(FeeConf_FeeBlockConfiguration_FeeBlockConfiguration_2) == E_OK)
    {
        Fee_WaitUntilIdle();
    }

    if (Fee_InvalidateBlock(FeeConf_FeeBlockConfiguration_FeeBlockConfiguration_1) == E_OK)
    {
        Fee_WaitUntilIdle();
    }
}
#endif
@endcode

@section fee_api API Quick Reference

@subsection fee_api_runtime Initialization & Runtime Control
| Function | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| Fee_Init() | Initialize the FEE runtime, FLS backend, and initial cluster scan. |
| Fee_MainFunction() | Advance the asynchronous state machine and backend flash work. |
| Fee_Cancel() | Cancel the currently active FEE job when the driver is busy. |

@subsection fee_api_status Job Status & Version Information
| Function | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| Fee_GetJobResult() | Return the result of the last accepted FEE job. |
| Fee_GetStatus() | Return the current MEMIF module state. |
| Fee_GetVersionInfo() | Return version metadata when `FEE_VERSION_INFO_API == STD_ON`. |

@subsection fee_api_data Data Transfer
| Function | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| Fee_Read() | Start an asynchronous read from a logical block. |
| Fee_Write() | Start an asynchronous write of a full logical block. |

@subsection fee_api_maint Block Maintenance
| Function | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| Fee_InvalidateBlock() | Mark the current logical block instance invalid in standard mode. |
| Fee_EraseImmediateBlock() | Re-prepare an immediate block for the next write in standard mode. |

@subsection fee_api_callbacks Flash Callback Hooks
| Function | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| Fee_JobEndNotification() | Continue the FEE state machine after a successful FLS step. |
| Fee_JobErrorNotification() | Enter the FEE error path after a failed FLS step. |

@section fee_notes Important Notes

@subsection fee_notes_async Asynchronous Completion Model
- `E_OK` from Fee_Read(), Fee_Write(), Fee_InvalidateBlock(), or
  Fee_EraseImmediateBlock() only means the request was accepted.
- Completion is reported through Fee_GetStatus() and Fee_GetJobResult() after
  Fee_MainFunction() advances the internal state machine.

@subsection fee_notes_callbacks Callback Wiring
- The FLS configuration passed through `flashConfigPtr` must use
  Fee_JobEndNotification() and Fee_JobErrorNotification() as its completion
  callbacks.
- If those callbacks are not wired correctly, scan, swap, write, and erase jobs
  cannot advance beyond the first flash transaction.

@subsection fee_notes_sizing Cluster and Reserved-Area Planning
- The effective storage demand of a cluster group includes block payload size,
  block header overhead, cluster header overhead, and `ReservedSize`.
- The configured cluster capacity must be large enough to hold the active data
  set plus any reserved space required by immediate blocks.

@subsection fee_notes_light Light-Mode Restrictions
- `Fee_InvalidateBlock()` and `Fee_EraseImmediateBlock()` are unavailable when
  `FEE_LIGHT_MODE == 1`.
- Light mode reduces metadata overhead and uses 24-bit address serialization,
  so migration between light mode and standard mode requires a dedicated flash
  reformat strategy.

@subsection fee_notes_buffers Buffer and Request Constraints
- Fee_Write() expects a buffer that contains the complete configured payload for
  the selected logical block.
- Fee_Read() offset and length parameters must stay inside the configured block
  size.
- The driver only accepts new requests while Fee_GetStatus() reports MEMIF_IDLE.

@section fee_integration Integration Guide

@subsection fee_integration_units Compilation Units
Compile the following source files into the project:
@verbatim
${SDK_PATH}/platform/drivers/src/fee/fee.c
${SDK_PATH}/platform/drivers/src/fee/fls_async_driver.c
${SDK_PATH}/platform/drivers/src/fee/fls_hw_access.c
@endverbatim

@subsection fee_integration_include Include Paths
Add the following include paths to the toolchain:
@verbatim
${SDK_PATH}/platform/drivers/inc
${SDK_PATH}/platform/drivers/src/fee
${SDK_PATH}/demos/<board>/fee/board
@endverbatim

@subsection fee_integration_symbols Compile Symbols
Common build-time options:
- `FEE_LIGHT_MODE=1` to enable the reduced-overhead light mode.
- `FEE_VERSION_INFO_API=STD_ON` to expose Fee_GetVersionInfo().

@subsection fee_integration_deps Dependencies
- Board-generated `fee_config.h` / `fee_config.c` with logical block, cluster,
  and FLS configuration objects.
- Periodic execution of Fee_MainFunction() from the system scheduler or super
  loop.
- Flash memory ranges dedicated to FEE storage and excluded from application
  code placement.

@}*/
